/-!
# `D_QCoh` of a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme has a perfect generator

[Stacks, Tag 09IS], the theorem of Bondal and Van den Bergh: on a quasi-compact quasi-separated
scheme `X` there is a perfect object `P` of `D(𝒪_X)` such that an object `E` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`
vanishes if and only if every morphism `P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E` vanishes.

The proof is the source's. It runs the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR] on the property of
a quasi-compact open `W ⊆ X` that `D_QCoh(𝒪_W)` has a perfect weak generator: the affine opens
are the base case, and the step passes from `U` quasi-compact and `V` affine to `U ∪ V`, with the
generator `Q ⊞ K` of
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop` — `Q` the
perfect extension of the generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_U)` along [Stacks, Tag 09IQ], and
`K = Rj_{V*}K_V` the pushforward of the Koszul object of equations cutting `(U ∪ V) ∖ U` out of
`V`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.HasPerfectGenerator` — the property of a scheme that
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is weakly generated by a single perfect object.
* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.HasPerfectGeneratorOn` — the property of an open `W` of `X` fed to
  the induction principle: *every* open subscheme of `X` whose image is `W` has a perfect
  generator.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_iso_spec` — the base case: a scheme
  isomorphic to `Spec A` has a perfect generator, namely the structure sheaf in degree zero in
  its Koszul spelling.
* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_two_opens` — the inductive step, for a
  scheme covered by a quasi-compact open `U` and an affine open `V` with equations cutting
  `X ∖ U` out of `V`.
* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs` and
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isZero_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero` are **[Stacks,
  Tag 09IS]**, the second in the source's own words.

## Implementation notes

**Why the induction runs on a property of the open subschemes rather than on `W.toScheme`.**
The inductive step has to be read inside `U ⊔ V`, so the induction hypothesis about `U` is needed
for the open `(U ⊔ V).ι ⁻¹ᵁ U` of `(U ⊔ V).toScheme`, which is isomorphic to `U.toScheme` but not
equal to it. Transporting the property along that isomorphism would ask for perfectness to be
carried along an isomorphism of schemes at the locally small model, which
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.isPerfect_derivedRestrict` does not provide — that statement installs
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` as a file-local instance and so speaks only about
the standard model. Quantifying over *all* open subschemes with a given image removes the need:
`(U ⊔ V).ι ⁻¹ᵁ U` composed with the inclusion of `U ⊔ V` is itself an open immersion into `X`
with image `U`, so the induction hypothesis applies to it directly, and the conclusion `P ⊤` is
read at the identity of `X`.

The one isomorphism that remains is in the base case, where the scheme is an arbitrary affine
one; there perfectness of the generator is
`Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isPerfect_derivedRestrict_koszulObject`, stated for an arbitrary open
immersion into `Spec A`, and the detection statement is carried across by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedRestrict_of_iso`, which is the
three-step argument of `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.RestrictComposite` — faithfulness,
reflection of the zero object, and reflection of Hom-vanishing — for restriction along an
isomorphism.

**The model is the locally small one** of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`:
no `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory` binder appears below, so instance search supplies the
global instances. This is forced. The base case passes through the affine derived Spec–Γ
equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], which is available at that model and at no other, and the
hypothesis that `Rj_*` preserves quasi-coherent cohomology is available there as
`Stacks.Duality.isQuasicoherent_homology_derivedPushforward_opens`; the
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` form
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedCategoryB_derivedPushforward_of_compactSpace` would not do.

That is a constraint on the *proof* and not on the conclusion:
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_anyModel` carries the
results below to an arbitrary chosen `D(𝒪_X)`, the standard model included, along the comparison
equivalence `StacksDraft.DerivedModel.modelEquiv` of two models.

**Generation inside the full subcategory and in the ambient category.**
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff` identifies the two, so
that the transports below can all be made in `D(𝒪_X)` while the statement of the tag stays inside
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes (IsPerfect)

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

/-- **Weak generation by a single object of a shift-stable full subcategory, read in the ambient
category.** For `E` an object of `A ⊆ C`, the singleton `{E}` is a weak generator of `A` exactly
when an object of `C` lying in `A` which receives only zero maps from the shifts of `E` is zero.

Both directions go through
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero`,
which writes right orthogonality to the shift closure of a singleton out as the vanishing of all
the morphisms. The inclusion of `A` is fully faithful and commutes with the shift, so it carries
the vanishing both ways —
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_ι` in one direction and
faithfulness in the other — and it reflects the zero object. -/
theorem isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff {C : Type*} [Category C] [Preadditive C]
    [HasShift C ℤ] (A : ObjectProperty C) [A.IsStableUnderShift ℤ] (E : A.FullSubcategory) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton E).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator ↔
      ∀ M : C, A M → (∀ (n : ℤ) (g : E.obj⟦n⟧ ⟶ M), g = 0) → IsZero M := by
  constructor
  · intro h M hM hzero
    have hz : IsZero (⟨M, hM⟩ : A.FullSubcategory) := by
      refine h _ ((rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero E _).2 ?_)
      intro n g
      refine A.fullyFaithfulι.map_injective ?_
      rw [A.ι.map_zero, ← cancel_epi ((A.ι.commShiftIso (A := ℤ) n).inv.app E), comp_zero]
      exact hzero n _
    exact A.ι.map_isZero hz
  · exact fun h K hK => Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_isZero_ι_obj A K
      (h K.obj K.2 ((rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero _ _).1
        (rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_ι A hK)))

/-- **A retract in a full subcategory, from a retract of the underlying objects.** The morphisms
of a full subcategory are the morphisms of the ambient category, but the identification is not
available to unification across the inclusion, so the two maps are transported by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.FullyFaithful.preimage` and the equation by faithfulness. -/
def retractOfι {C : Type*} [Category C] (A : ObjectProperty C) {X Y : A.FullSubcategory}
    (i : A.ι.obj X ⟶ A.ι.obj Y) (p : A.ι.obj Y ⟶ A.ι.obj X) (h : i ≫ p = 𝟙 (A.ι.obj X)) :
    Retract X Y where
  i := A.fullyFaithfulι.preimage i
  r := A.fullyFaithfulι.preimage p
  retract := A.fullyFaithfulι.map_injective <| by
    rwa [A.ι.map_comp, A.fullyFaithfulι.map_preimage, A.fullyFaithfulι.map_preimage, A.ι.map_id]

end CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

namespace Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel

/-! ### The property of having a perfect generator -/

/-- **`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` has a perfect weak generator**: there is an object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` which is
perfect as an object of `D(𝒪_X)` and whose singleton is a weak generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`.

This is the property [Stacks, Tag 09IS] asserts of a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme. -/
def HasPerfectGenerator (X : Scheme.{u}) : Prop :=
  ∃ E : Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X,
    IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) E.obj ∧
      (ObjectProperty.singleton E).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator

/-- `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` is a triangulated subcategory of `D(𝒪_Y)`. -/
private instance isTriangulated_derivedCategoryB_isQuasicoherent (Y : Scheme.{u}) :
    (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := Y.Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent Y.ringCatSheaf)).IsTriangulated :=
  DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB_isTriangulated _
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre.isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre Y)

/-- **A biproduct of two perfect objects of a triangulated subcategory of `D(𝒪_Y)` is perfect.**
The biproduct is the second vertex of the split triangle on its two summands, the inclusion of a
triangulated subcategory carries that triangle to a distinguished triangle of `D(𝒪_Y)`, and
[Stacks, Tag 08CR] gives perfectness of the second vertex. -/
theorem isPerfect_biprod_fullSubcategory {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (A : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory Y.Modules)) [A.IsTriangulated] (Q K : A.FullSubcategory)
    (hQ : IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace) (A.ι.obj Q))
    (hK : IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace) (A.ι.obj K)) :
    IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace) (A.ι.obj (Q ⊞ K)) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_obj₂_of_distinguished _
    (A.ι.map_distinguished _
      (CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.binaryBiproductTriangle_distinguished Q K)) hQ hK

/-! ### The base case: a scheme isomorphic to a spectrum -/

/-- **Detection of the zero object travels along an isomorphism of schemes.** Let `e : Y ≅ Z` and
let `K` be an object of `D(𝒪_Z)` detecting the zero object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)`, in the sense that an
object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)` receiving only zero maps from the shifts of `K` is zero. Then `K|_Y`
detects the zero object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`.

Restricting `M` along `e.inv` lands in `D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)`
(`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedCategoryB_derivedRestrict`); restriction along `e.hom` is
faithful and commutes with the shift, so it reflects the vanishing of the morphisms out of all
shifts of an object (`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful`); and it
reflects the zero object
(`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isZero_of_isZero_derivedRestrict_of_compEqId`). -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedRestrict_of_iso {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (e : Y ≅ Z)
    (K : DerivedCategory Z.Modules)
    (hdet : ∀ N : DerivedCategory Z.Modules,
      DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := Z.Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent Z.ringCatSheaf) N →
      (∀ (n : ℤ) (g : K⟦n⟧ ⟶ N), g = 0) → IsZero N)
    (M : DerivedCategory Y.Modules)
    (hM : DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := Y.Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent Y.ringCatSheaf) M)
    (h : ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.hom).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)⟦n⟧ ⟶ M),
      g = 0) :
    IsZero M := by
  let := faithful_derivedRestrict_of_compEqId e.inv e.hom e.inv_hom_id
  refine isZero_of_isZero_derivedRestrict_of_compEqId e.hom e.inv e.hom_inv_id
    (hdet _ (Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedCategoryB_derivedRestrict e.inv M hM) ?_)
  exact forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.hom).mapDerivedCategory
    ((derivedRestrictCompIsoId e.hom e.inv e.hom_inv_id).app M) h

/-- **The base case of the induction of [Stacks, Tag 09IS]: a scheme isomorphic to `Spec A` has a
perfect generator.** The generator is the Koszul object of the empty sequence in `A`, read on `Y`
along the isomorphism; it is the structure sheaf of `Y` in degree zero.

It is perfect by `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isPerfect_derivedRestrict_koszulObject` and lies in
`D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` because a perfect object does. That it generates is
`Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero` — the affine case of
[Stacks, Tag 09IS], which is [Stacks, Tag 09IR] for the empty sequence — carried across the
isomorphism by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedRestrict_of_iso`. -/
theorem hasPerfectGenerator_of_iso_spec {Y : Scheme.{u}} {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (e : Y ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) : HasPerfectGenerator Y := by
  have hEperf : IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace)
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.hom).mapDerivedCategory.obj
        (Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject (fun i : Fin 0 => i.elim0))) :=
    Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isPerfect_derivedRestrict_koszulObject _ e.hom
  refine ⟨⟨_, Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isDQCoh_of_isPerfect
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory Y) _ hEperf⟩, hEperf, ?_⟩
  exact (ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff _ _).2
    (isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedRestrict_of_iso e _
      (Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero
        (fun i : Fin 0 => i.elim0)))

/-! ### The inductive step: two opens, one of them affine -/

/-- **The inductive step of [Stacks, Tag 09IS].** Let `Y` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated
scheme covered by a quasi-compact open `U` and an open `V` presented by an isomorphism
`e : V ≅ Spec A`, and let `f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` cut `Y ∖ U` out of `V`. If `D_QCoh(𝒪_U)` has a perfect
generator then so does `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`.

The generator is `Q ⊞ K` of
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop` at
`A = D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` and `B = D_QCoh(𝒪_U)`, whose hypotheses are discharged as follows. `Q` is the
perfect object of `D(𝒪_Y)` restricting to a retract of the generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_U)`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 09IQ]; `K = Rj_{V*}K_V` is the pushforward of the Koszul object, perfect by
[Stacks, Tag 08DP] and with its two geometric hypotheses `hKzero` and `hdet` supplied by
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedQCoh/KoszulDetectionTwoOpens.lean`; `hres` is preservation
of quasi-coherence by restriction and `hpush` preservation by `Rj_*`, part (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 08D5]; the counit is invertible because `Rj_*` along an open immersion is fully
faithful; and the closure of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` under cones is
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedCategoryB_obj₃_of_distTriang`. Perfectness of the biproduct is
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isPerfect_biprod_fullSubcategory`. -/
theorem hasPerfectGenerator_of_two_opens {Y : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace Y]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] (U V : Y.Opens) [CompactSpace U.toScheme] {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (e : V.toScheme ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (hf : e.hom ⁻¹ᵁ Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.openComplement f = V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U) (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤)
    (hPU : HasPerfectGenerator U.toScheme) : HasPerfectGenerator Y := by
  obtain ⟨P, hPperf, hPgen⟩ := hPU
  obtain ⟨R, hRperf, i, p, hip⟩ := exists_isPerfect_retract_derivedRestrict U
    (isCompact_iff_compactSpace.2 ‹_›) P.obj hPperf
  have hKperf : IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace)
      ((Stacks.Duality.derivedPushforward V.ι).obj (Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.koszulObjectOn V e f)) :=
    Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isPerfect_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn U V e f hf hUV
  have hQmem := isDQCoh_of_isPerfect (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory Y) R
    hRperf
  have hKmem := Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.derivedQuasiCoherent_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn
    U V e f hf hUV
  refine ⟨(⟨R, hQmem⟩ : _) ⊞ (⟨_, hKmem⟩ : _), ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact isPerfect_biprod_fullSubcategory _ _ _ hRperf hKperf
  · refine Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop
      U.ι (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := Y.Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent Y.ringCatSheaf))
      (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := U.toScheme.Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf))
      (fun N => Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedCategoryB_derivedRestrict U.ι N.obj N.2)
      (fun L n => Stacks.Duality.isQuasicoherent_homology_derivedPushforward_opens U L n)
      AlgebraicGeometry.derivedCategoryB_obj₃_of_distTriang ?_ hPgen
      (Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn U V e f hf)
      (fun _ => inferInstance)
      (Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn
        U V e f hf hUV)
    exact ObjectProperty.retractOfι _ i p hip

/-! ### The induction -/

/-- **The property of an open `W` of `X` that the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR] is run
on**: every open subscheme of `X` with image `W` has a perfect generator.

Quantifying over all open immersions with image `W`, rather than naming `W.toScheme`, is what
makes the inductive step need no transport of perfectness along an isomorphism of schemes; see
the implementation notes of this file. -/
def HasPerfectGeneratorOn {X : Scheme.{u}} (W : X.Opens) : Prop :=
  ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (h : Y ⟶ X), IsOpenImmersion h → Set.range h.base = (W : Set X) →
    HasPerfectGenerator Y

/-- An open immersion of schemes whose image is quasi-compact has a quasi-compact source: its
base map is an embedding, and it carries the whole space onto that image. -/
theorem compactSpace_of_range_isCompact {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (h : Y ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion h]
    (hc : IsCompact (Set.range h.base)) : CompactSpace Y := by
  rw [← isCompact_univ_iff]
  exact h.isOpenEmbedding.isEmbedding.isCompact_iff.2 (by rwa [Set.image_univ])

/-- The preimage of a quasi-compact open contained in the image of an open immersion is
quasi-compact: the base map is an embedding and carries that preimage onto the open. -/
theorem isCompact_preimage_of_subset_range {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (h : Y ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion h]
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsCompact (U : Set X)) (hle : (U : Set X) ⊆ Set.range h.base) :
    IsCompact ((h ⁻¹ᵁ U : Y.Opens) : Set Y) := by
  refine h.isOpenEmbedding.isEmbedding.isCompact_iff.2 ?_
  simpa [Set.image_preimage_eq_of_subset hle] using hU

/-- The image of the open immersion `(h ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ h` is `U`, for `h` an open immersion whose
image contains `U`. This is what lets the induction hypothesis about `U` be applied to the open
`h ⁻¹ᵁ U` of the source of `h`. -/
theorem range_preimage_ι_comp {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (h : Y ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion h] (U : X.Opens)
    (hle : (U : Set X) ⊆ Set.range h.base) :
    Set.range ((h ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ h).base = (U : Set X) := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_base, TopCat.coe_comp, Set.range_comp, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
  simpa using Set.image_preimage_eq_of_subset hle

/-- **The base clause of the induction**: an open subscheme of `X` whose image is an affine open
is an affine scheme, so `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_iso_spec` applies to
it through the composite of the comparison with `W.toScheme` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isoSpec`. -/
theorem hasPerfectGeneratorOn_of_isAffineOpen {X : Scheme.{u}} (W : X.Opens)
    (hW : IsAffineOpen W) : HasPerfectGeneratorOn W := by
  intro Y h _ hrange
  have : IsAffine W.toScheme := hW
  exact hasPerfectGenerator_of_iso_spec (A := (Γ(X, W) : Type u))
    (IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq h W.ι (by rw [hrange, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]) ≪≫ hW.isoSpec)

/-- **The inductive clause of the induction**: the property passes from a quasi-compact open `U`
and an affine open `V` to `U ⊔ V`.

Let `h : Y ⟶ X` be an open immersion with image `U ⊔ V`. Then `Y` is quasi-compact and
quasi-separated, the opens `h ⁻¹ᵁ U` and `h ⁻¹ᵁ V` cover it, the first is quasi-compact and the
second is isomorphic to `V.toScheme` and hence to `Spec Γ(X, V)`, and the induction hypothesis
applies to `(h ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ h`, whose image is `U`. The equations cutting `Y ∖ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U)` out of
`h ⁻¹ᵁ V` come from `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.OpenLift.exists_unionOfBasicOpens_eq` applied to the
image of `(h ⁻¹ᵁ V) ∩ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U)` in `Spec Γ(X, V)`, a quasi-compact open because `Y` is
quasi-separated; `AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine` turns the resulting union of
principal opens into the `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.openComplement` spelling.
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_two_opens` then applies. -/
theorem hasPerfectGeneratorOn_sup {X : Scheme.{u}} [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] (U V : X.Opens)
    (hU : IsCompact (U : Set X)) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hPU : HasPerfectGeneratorOn U) :
    HasPerfectGeneratorOn (U ⊔ V) := by
  intro Y h _ hrange
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace Y := QuasiSeparatedSpace.of_isOpenEmbedding h.isOpenEmbedding
  have : IsAffine V.toScheme := hV
  have hle : ∀ W : X.Opens, W ≤ U ⊔ V → (W : Set X) ⊆ Set.range h.base := fun W hW => by
    rw [hrange]
    exact hW
  have hUle := hle U le_sup_left
  have hVle := hle V le_sup_right
  have hUc := isCompact_preimage_of_subset_range h U hU hUle
  have hVc := isCompact_preimage_of_subset_range h V hV.isCompact hVle
  have : CompactSpace Y := compactSpace_of_range_isCompact h <| by
    rw [hrange, Opens.coe_sup]
    exact hU.union hV.isCompact
  have : CompactSpace (h ⁻¹ᵁ U).toScheme := isCompact_iff_compactSpace.1 hUc
  have : CompactSpace (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme := isCompact_iff_compactSpace.1 hVc
  have hiso : (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme ≅ V.toScheme :=
    IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq ((h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ h) V.ι (by
      rw [range_preimage_ι_comp h V hVle, Scheme.Opens.range_ι])
  have : IsAffine (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme := IsAffine.of_isIso hiso.hom
  have hcover : (h ⁻¹ᵁ U) ⊔ (h ⁻¹ᵁ V) = (⊤ : Y.Opens) := by
    ext y
    have hy : h.base y ∈ Set.range h.base := ⟨y, rfl⟩
    rw [hrange] at hy
    simp only [Opens.coe_sup, Set.mem_union] at hy
    simpa using hy
  have hc : IsCompact ((((h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U)) : (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme.Opens) :
      Set (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme) := by
    refine (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι.isOpenEmbedding.isEmbedding.isCompact_iff.2 ?_
    have himg : (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι.base '' ((((h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U)) : (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme.Opens) :
        Set (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme)
        = ((h ⁻¹ᵁ U : Y.Opens) : Set Y) ∩ ((h ⁻¹ᵁ V : Y.Opens) : Set Y) := by
      simp [Set.image_preimage_eq_inter_range]
    rw [himg]
    exact QuasiSeparatedSpace.inter_isCompact _ _ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U).2 hUc (h ⁻¹ᵁ V).2 hVc
  have hZc : IsCompact ((((hiso ≪≫ hV.isoSpec).hom ''ᵁ
      ((h ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (h ⁻¹ᵁ U))) : (Spec Γ(X, V)).Opens) : Set (Spec Γ(X, V))) := by
    simpa [Set.image_image] using
      hc.image (hiso ≪≫ hV.isoSpec).hom.isOpenEmbedding.continuous
  obtain ⟨r, f, hrf⟩ := Stacks.DerivedQCoh.OpenLift.exists_unionOfBasicOpens_eq _ hZc
  refine hasPerfectGenerator_of_two_opens (h ⁻¹ᵁ U) (h ⁻¹ᵁ V) (hiso ≪≫ hV.isoSpec) f ?_ hcover
    (hPU _ ((h ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ h) inferInstance (range_preimage_ι_comp h U hUle))
  rw [show Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.openComplement f
      = Koszul.DerivedSystem.unionOfBasicOpens (A := Γ(X, V)) f from
    iSup_congr fun i => AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine (R := Γ(X, V)) (f i), hrf]
  exact (hiso ≪≫ hV.isoSpec).hom.preimage_image_eq _

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 09IS], the theorem of Bondal and Van den Bergh**, in the form that
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is weakly generated by a single perfect object: on a quasi-compact quasi-separated
scheme the property `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.HasPerfectGenerator` holds.

This is the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR] — in the clause `induction_top` for the whole
space — applied to `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.HasPerfectGeneratorOn`, whose two clauses are
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGeneratorOn_of_isAffineOpen` and
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGeneratorOn_sup`; the conclusion is read at the identity
of `X`, an open immersion whose image is all of `X`. -/
@[stacks 09IS "the generator, in the ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator spelling"]
theorem hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] :
    HasPerfectGenerator X :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InductionPrinciple.induction_top (X := X) HasPerfectGeneratorOn
    hasPerfectGeneratorOn_of_isAffineOpen
    (fun U V hU hV hPU _ _ => hasPerfectGeneratorOn_sup U V hU hV hPU)
    X (𝟙 X) inferInstance (by simp)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 09IS], the theorem of Bondal and Van den Bergh, in the source's own words.**
Let `X` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme. There is a perfect object `P` of `D(𝒪_X)` such
that for every object `E` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` the following are equivalent: `E = 0`, and
`Hom_{D(𝒪_X)}(P⟦n⟧, E) = 0` for all `n : ℤ`.

This is `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs` read in the ambient derived
category by `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff`; the
converse implication holds for any object, a morphism into a zero object being zero. -/
@[stacks 09IS]
theorem exists_isPerfect_isZero_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] :
    ∃ P : DerivedCategory X.Modules, IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) P ∧
      ∀ E : DerivedCategory X.Modules, DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := X.Modules)
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) E →
          (IsZero E ↔ ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E), g = 0) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hEperf, hEgen⟩ := hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs X
  exact ⟨E.obj, hEperf, fun M hM => ⟨fun hz n g => hz.eq_of_tgt _ _,
    (ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff _ E).1 hEgen M hM⟩⟩

end Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel

